  "title": "tpm20: fix CC_NVRead parseing missing authHandle",
  "description": "# TPM2.0 Dissector: Incorrect Handle Count for TPM2_CC_NV_Read Command\n\n## Summary\nThe TPM 2.0 protocol dissector (`packet-tpm20.c`) incorrectly specifies the number of request handles for the `TPM2_CC_NV_Read` command (0x14e), causing improper dissection of NV_Read command packets.\n\n## Description\nThe current implementation defines `TPM2_CC_NV_Read` with only 1 request handle, when according to the TPM 2.0 specification (Part 3: Commands, Section 31.13) https://trustedcomputinggroup.org/wp-content/uploads/Trusted-Platform-Module-2.0-Library-Part-3-Version-184_pub.pdf , this command requires 2 handles:\n\n1. **authHandle** - Handle indicating the source of the authorisation value\n2. **nvIndex** - The NV Index to be read\n\nThis causes the dissector to fail to properly decode the handle area of NV_Read commands, potentially misinterpreting subsequent fields in the packet.\n\n## Expected Behaviour\nThe dissector should recognise and decode both handles for `TPM2_CC_NV_Read` commands, consistent with:\n- The TPM 2.0 specification\n- Other similar NV commands in the dissector (NV_Increment, NV_SetBits, NV_Extend, NV_Write)\n- The implementation in related projects (e.g., tpmstream: https://github.com/joholl/tpmstream/commit/2597e6d5a88b735a371090cf1f9bc2ddbd8f563c)\n\nThis change:\n- Corrects the handle count from 1 to 2\n- Specifies both required handle fields: `hf_tpmi_rh_nv_auth` and `hf_tpmi_rh_nv_index`\n- Makes the definition consistent with other NV commands that use both auth and index handles\n\n## Reference\n- TPM 2.0 Specification Part 3: Commands, Section 31.13 (TPM2_NV_Read):\nhttps://trustedcomputinggroup.org/wp-content/uploads/Trusted-Platform-Module-2.0-Library-Part-3-Version-184_pub.pdf\n- Similar fix in tpmstream project: https://github.com/joholl/tpmstream/commit/2597e6d5a88b735a371090cf1f9bc2ddbd8f563c\n\n## Additional Context\nThe pattern for 2-handle NV commands is already correctly implemented elsewhere in the dissector:\n- `CC_NV_Increment` (0x134)\n- `CC_NV_SetBits` (0x135) \n- `CC_NV_Extend` (0x136)\n- `CC_NV_Write` (0x137)\n- `CC_NV_ReadLock` (0x14f)\n\nAll use the same handle field types as proposed for the fix.\n\n## Testcase\nThe attached PCAP is from a windows 10 VM in QEMU using SWTPM with bitlocker configured in TPM only mode. Frame 77 is an NV_Read which does not currently decode properly.[win10-swtpm-boot.pcap](/uploads/68719dc923643d8478dfc3c346199c2a/win10-swtpm-boot.pcap)",
